2. Mathematical Preliminaries

Notation

· \mathbb{R}, \mathbb{R}_{\ge 0}: real numbers, non-negative reals.
· \mathbb{E}[\cdot]: expectation. \Pr(\cdot): probability.
· \mathcal{N}(\mu,\Sigma): multivariate normal distribution.
· \|x\|: Euclidean norm.
· For a set S, \text{int}(S) interior, \partial S boundary.
· \Sigma[x]: the set of sum-of-squares polynomials in variables x.

Definition 2.1 (Stochastic Hybrid System)

A stochastic hybrid system is a tuple

\mathcal{H} = (Q, X, U, f, g, \text{Inv}, \text{Guard}, \text{Reset}, \sigma),

where Q is a finite set of discrete modes, X \subset \mathbb{R}^n continuous state space, U \subset \mathbb{R}^m control input space, f: Q \times X \times U \to \mathbb{R}^n drift, g: Q \times X \times U \to \mathbb{R}^{n \times p} diffusion, \text{Inv}: Q \to 2^X invariants, \text{Guard}: Q \times Q \to 2^X guards, \text{Reset}: Q \times Q \times X \to X reset maps, and \sigma a p-dimensional Wiener process. Continuous dynamics in mode q:

dx(t) = f(q,x(t),u(t))\,dt + g(q,x(t),u(t))\,dW(t).

Discrete transitions occur when x(t) hits a guard; the state jumps according to Reset and mode changes.

Definition 2.2 (Stochastic Barrier Certificate for Hybrid Systems)

Given a stochastic hybrid system \mathcal{H}, an unsafe set X_u \subset X, and an initial set X_0 \subset X, a family of twice differentiable functions B_q: X \to \mathbb{R}_{\ge 0}, one per mode q \in Q, is a stochastic barrier certificate if there exist constants \eta > 0, c \ge 0 such that for all modes q, q' \in Q:

B_q(x) \le c \quad \forall x \in X_0 \cap \text{Inv}(q),

B_q(x) \ge \eta \quad \forall x \in X_u \cap \text{Inv}(q),

\mathcal{L}_q B_q(x) \le 0 \quad \forall x \in \text{Inv}(q),

B_{q'}\bigl(\text{Reset}(q,q',x)\bigr) \le B_q(x) \quad \forall x \in \text{Guard}(q,q'),

where \mathcal{L}_q is the infinitesimal generator in mode q:

\mathcal{L}_q B = \frac{\partial B}{\partial x} f_q + \frac{1}{2}\text{Tr}\left( g_q g_q^\top \frac{\partial^2 B}{\partial x^2} \right).

This definition ensures B_{q(t)}(x_t) is a nonnegative supermartingale across both continuous evolution and discrete transitions. The probability of reaching X_u from X_0 is bounded by c/\eta via Doob's maximal inequality.

Definition 2.3 (Sum-of-Squares Polynomial)

A polynomial p(x) \in \mathbb{R}[x] is sum-of-squares if p(x) = \sum_{i=1}^r q_i(x)^2 for some polynomials q_i. SOS membership is equivalent to a semidefinite programming feasibility problem.

Definition 2.4 (Chance Constraint)

A constraint \Pr(h(x) \le 0) \ge 1-\varepsilon is a chance constraint. In robust MPC, it is often replaced by a deterministic robust constraint under bounded disturbance.

