For the tube MPC, the disturbance set \mathcal{W} is constructed as follows:

1. Process noise: The Gaussian noise terms \sigma_T, \sigma_M, \sigma_{pH}, \sigma_{a_w} are bounded using the Gaussian tail bound (Lemma A.8) at a specified confidence level.
2. Polynomial approximation error: The error bounds \Delta k from the certified polynomial approximation are included as deterministic bounded disturbances.
3. Digital twin prediction error: The conformal prediction threshold \hat{q}_t is used to enlarge the disturbance set online.

The combined disturbance set is:

\mathcal{W} = \{ w \in \mathbb{R}^n : |w_i| \le \gamma_i \hat{\sigma}_i + \Delta_i + \hat{q}_i \},

where \gamma_i is chosen to achieve the desired confidence level, \hat{\sigma}_i is the estimated noise standard deviation, \Delta_i is the approximation error bound, and \hat{q}_i is the conformal prediction threshold.

E.3 Terminal Set Design

The terminal set \mathcal{X}_f is designed as a sublevel set of a robust local Control Lyapunov–Barrier function V_f(x):

\mathcal{X}_f = \{ x \in \mathcal{X} : V_f(x) \le \alpha \},

where V_f and the local policy \kappa_f are co-designed via SOS programming to satisfy:

V_f(F(x, \kappa_f(x), w)) \le V_f(x) \quad \forall x \in \mathcal{X}_f, \ w \in \mathcal{W},

V_f(x) \ge \eta_f \quad \forall x \in X_u.

The SOS constraints are:

V_f(x) - \alpha \in \Sigma[x] \quad \text{on } \mathcal{X},

V_f(F(x, \kappa_f(x), 0)) - V_f(x) + \sum_i \lambda_i(x) (w_i^2 - \bar{w}_i^2) \in \Sigma[x, w],

V_f(x) - \eta_f \in \Sigma[x] \quad \text{on } X_u.

