Appendix F: Detailed SOS Formulations

F.1 Barrier Certificate Synthesis for Heating Mode

Consider the heating mode with dynamics:

\begin{aligned}
dT &= \alpha (T_{\text{set}} - T) dt + \sigma_T dW_T, \\
dM &= -\frac{\tilde{k}_{\text{therm}}(T, pH, a_w)}{\ln 10} dt + e(x) dt + \sigma_M dW_M, \\
dpH &= 0, \\
da_w &= 0,
\end{aligned}

where \tilde{k}_{\text{therm}} is the polynomial approximation of the Bigelow rate, and e(x) \in [-\Delta k/\ln 10, \Delta k/\ln 10].

The infinitesimal generator is:

\mathcal{L}_{\text{heat}} B = \frac{\partial B}{\partial T} \alpha (T_{\text{set}} - T) - \frac{\partial B}{\partial M} \frac{\tilde{k}_{\text{therm}}}{\ln 10} + \frac{1}{2} \sigma_T^2 \frac{\partial^2 B}{\partial T^2} + \frac{1}{2} \sigma_M^2 \frac{\partial^2 B}{\partial M^2}.

The SOS constraint for the drift condition with disturbance is:

-\mathcal{L}_{\text{heat}} B(x) - \lambda(x) (e^2 - \Delta^2) \in \Sigma[x, e],

where \Delta = \Delta k / \ln 10 and \lambda(x) \in \Sigma[x, e].

F.2 Barrier Certificate Synthesis for Storage Mode

Consider the storage mode with dynamics:

\begin{aligned}
dM &= \frac{\tilde{\mu}_{\max}(a_w, T, pH)}{\ln 10} \cdot (1 - 10^{M - M_{\max}}) dt + \sigma_{M,\text{storage}} dW_M, \\
dT &= \sigma_{T,\text{storage}} dW_T, \\
da_w &= \sigma_{a_w,\text{storage}} dW_{a_w}, \\
dpH &= 0.
\end{aligned}

The infinitesimal generator is:

\mathcal{L}_{\text{store}} B = \frac{\partial B}{\partial M} \frac{\tilde{\mu}_{\max}}{\ln 10} (1 - 10^{M - M_{\max}}) + \frac{1}{2} \sigma_{M,\text{storage}}^2 \frac{\partial^2 B}{\partial M^2} + \frac{1}{2} \sigma_{T,\text{storage}}^2 \frac{\partial^2 B}{\partial T^2} + \frac{1}{2} \sigma_{a_w,\text{storage}}^2 \frac{\partial^2 B}{\partial a_w^2}.

The SOS constraint is:

-\mathcal{L}_{\text{store}} B(x) - \lambda(x) (e^2 - \Delta^2) \in \Sigma[x, e],

where e is the approximation error in \tilde{\mu}_{\max}.

F.3 Reset Conditions

For the transition from heating to acidification, the reset map is:

\text{Reset}(\text{heat}, \text{acid}, x) = [T, pH, a_w, M, N, \theta]^\top,

i.e., the state is continuous across this transition. The reset condition is:

B_{\text{acid}}(x) - B_{\text{heat}}(x) \in \Sigma[x] \quad \text{on } \text{Guard}(\text{heat}, \text{acid}).

For the transition from acidification to drying, the reset is also continuous, and the condition is similar.

For the transition from drying to storage (packaging), the reset is:

\text{Reset}(\text{dry}, \text{store}, x) = [T_{\text{pack}}, pH, a_w, M, N, \theta]^\top,

where T_{\text{pack}} is the packaging temperature. The reset condition is:

B_{\text{store}}(T_{\text{pack}}, pH, a_w, M, N, \theta) - B_{\text{dry}}(T, pH, a_w, M, N, \theta) \in \Sigma[x] \quad \text{on } \text{Guard}(\text{dry}, \text{store}).

